# Intent: <title>

## Problem

What cannot be done today, or what goes wrong, and for whom. Describe the situation — not the
solution. One or two short paragraphs; a concrete example beats an abstract statement.

## Proposed outcome

What "better" looks like from the point of view of the people affected. State the observable
result, not how to build it.

## Affected users and systems

- **Users / roles:** who notices the problem today and who will notice the change
- **Systems:** the products, screens, services, or integrations likely to be involved (name what
  you know; "not sure" is an acceptable answer)

## Constraints

Anything that must stay true: policy, security, compliance, budget, timing, things that must not
change. If none are known, say so explicitly.

## Open questions

Questions the originator could not answer and who might. The next stage (`/requirement-intake`
or `/prd`) must answer or carry forward every item here. If this intent is `closed`, the reason
goes here.
